<p>Two quick points on an otherwise pretty excellent post&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If left alone, subjects will die of dehydration within 74 hours.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems a little&#8230; arbitrary?</p>
<p>I think this can be shortened to:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If left alone, subjects will die of dehydration.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>If the subject is forced to assume a seated or prone position, or if SCP-2274 is removed from a subject’s line of sight, the subject will react violently, attacking whomever is instigating the change (See Interview Log 2274-1). No supernatural strength or unusual speed has been observed in subjects during these outbursts.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How long does this last?</p>
<p>It would be relatively easy to expose a Class D and then physically remove them from the presence of the statue&#8230; is there some reason no testing is allowed?</p>

